From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: bound capture control requests and isolate HAL/TCC

STEAMAC-8N reports PCM_START (0x104) timeout for hw:0c before the
HELLDIVERS 2 frame stall; STEAMAC-8P retains 4096 capture queue errors.
The baseline also reproduces on the development M1 Max: arecord times
out START, STOP, RELEASE; sampling finds the virtio-snd worker stuck in
HostStream::configure -> AudioUnitSetProperty -> HALC_ProxyObject RPC,
with the shared playback pump blocked behind its hosts mutex.

Move capture device calls to one bounded-command worker, independent of
playback. Return IO_ERR after 200 ms instead of losing the control queue
while a HAL call or microphone permission prompt waits. Cancel late starts,
make STOP nonblocking, and return capture descriptors on RELEASE even if
HAL is still stuck (including RX descriptors processed after RELEASE).
Log input-device identity, microphone permission, and setup results.
Known denied/restricted permission fails without starting the audio unit.

The capture scheduler integration tests use a deliberately blocked device
call, exercise cancellation and failure completion without microphone/TCC.
The game freeze itself is not proven to have an audio-only cause.
